"Spatial energy body of the speaker feeds. Its radius in each direction is the level heard from there, from %@ dBFS at the listener to 0 dBFS at the speakers, not a distance. Energy several speakers carry coherently points between them; energy out of phase is tinted ochre. Height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation." = "Spatial energy body of the speaker feeds. Its radius in each direction is the level heard from there, from %@ dBFS at the listener to 0 dBFS at the speakers, not a distance. Energy several speakers carry coherently points between them; energy out of phase is tinted ochre. Height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation.";
"The body shows how loud the speaker feeds are heard from each direction: its radius is the level in dBFS (the rings on the floor), not a distance. Energy only one speaker carries points at that speaker. Energy several speakers carry coherently points between them, where its phantom image is heard: along their velocity vector below about 700 Hz and their energy vector above (Gerzon), as wide as the energy vector predicts it is heard (Frank). Energy that cancels between speakers has no stable direction: it spreads wide and is tinted ochre. An estimate from the feeds, not a measured sound field; height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation. Hover over the body to read a direction's level and what forms it." = "The body shows how loud the speaker feeds are heard from each direction: its radius is the level in dBFS (the rings on the floor), not a distance. Energy only one speaker carries points at that speaker. Energy several speakers carry coherently points between them, where its phantom image is heard: along their velocity vector below about 700 Hz and their energy vector above (Gerzon), as wide as the energy vector predicts it is heard (Frank). Energy that cancels between speakers has no stable direction: it spreads wide and is tinted ochre. An estimate from the feeds, not a measured sound field; height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation. Hover over the body to read a direction's level and what forms it.";
