"How far below the loudest band particles still glow, in dB: the loudest burn white, quieter ones fade out over this range. How loud the loudest band is sets how bright the whole glow is. Hover over a particle to read its band's level." = "How far below the loudest band particles still glow, in dB: the loudest burn white, quieter ones fade out over this range. How loud the loudest band is sets how bright the whole glow is. Hover over a particle to read its band's level.";
"The quietest band drawn: a band below it sends no particles, whatever the glow range." = "The quietest band drawn: a band below it sends no particles, whatever the glow range.";
"Frequency colors each band's particles by its frequency, warm bass through cool treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white. Theme draws them in the palette's color. A split into 3 or 5 bands always shows each band in its own color." = "Frequency colors each band's particles by its frequency, warm bass through cool treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white. Theme draws them in the palette's color. A split into 3 or 5 bands always shows each band in its own color.";
"Each particle wears its band's color, warm for bass and cool for treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white." = "Each particle wears its band's color, warm for bass and cool for treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white.";
"Radiant draws each band as particles where its frequencies are heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry them, weighted by their level in each, so a centred phantom is a bright point between L and R and a wide stereo programme a streak along the line between them. The particles glow in their frequency's hue, as bright as they are loud, then fade and smear as they age. Level body draws the level heard from each direction as the radius of one body, read on the floor's dBFS rings." = "Radiant draws each band as particles where its frequencies are heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry them, weighted by their level in each, so a centred phantom is a bright point between L and R and a wide stereo programme a streak along the line between them. The particles glow in their frequency's hue, as bright as they are loud, then fade and smear as they age. Level body draws the level heard from each direction as the radius of one body, read on the floor's dBFS rings.";
"Each particle is one of a band's frequencies in the newest analysis, where it is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers, weighted by its amplitude in each. A sound only one speaker carries sits at that speaker; one panned between speakers sits on the line between them where its gains put it, at every frequency; two sounds sharing a band each keep their own place; sound the speakers carry independently scatters along the lines between them, frequency by frequency. Energy that cancels between speakers is tinted ochre where it sits. An estimate from the feeds, not a measured sound field; height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation. Hover over a particle to read its band, level and what places it there." = "Each particle is one of a band's frequencies in the newest analysis, where it is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers, weighted by its amplitude in each. A sound only one speaker carries sits at that speaker; one panned between speakers sits on the line between them where its gains put it, at every frequency; two sounds sharing a band each keep their own place; sound the speakers carry independently scatters along the lines between them, frequency by frequency. Energy that cancels between speakers is tinted ochre where it sits. An estimate from the feeds, not a measured sound field; height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation. Hover over a particle to read its band, level and what places it there.";
"How readily speakers that share coherent energy count as one image. In Radiant it decides what reads as a phantom image or out of phase (the ochre tint and the pointer's reading), not where particles sit: their frequencies' amplitudes decide that. Coherence is measured from the speakers' smoothed cross-spectra and corrected for chance. The analysis uses it (in the plugin, too)." = "How readily speakers that share coherent energy count as one image. In Radiant it decides what reads as a phantom image or out of phase (the ochre tint and the pointer's reading), not where particles sit: their frequencies' amplitudes decide that. Coherence is measured from the speakers' smoothed cross-spectra and corrected for chance. The analysis uses it (in the plugin, too).";
"This plugin sends no frequencies of its own (before build 87), so Radiant draws its particles from the spatial field's statistics. Install the plugins of this build to see each frequency where it is heard." = "This plugin sends no frequencies of its own (before build 87), so Radiant draws its particles from the spatial field's statistics. Install the plugins of this build to see each frequency where it is heard.";
"Particles of the speaker feeds' frequency bands, each where its band is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry it, weighted by its level in each. A centred phantom is a bright point between two speakers, a wide stereo programme a streak along the line between them, sound all round gathers toward the listener. The loudest band glows white and quieter ones fade out %d dB below it; particles fade and smear as they age. Energy out of phase scatters and is tinted ochre. Height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation." = "Particles of the speaker feeds' frequency bands, each where its band is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry it, weighted by its level in each. A centred phantom is a bright point between two speakers, a wide stereo programme a streak along the line between them, sound all round gathers toward the listener. The loudest band glows white and quieter ones fade out %d dB below it; particles fade and smear as they age. Energy out of phase scatters and is tinted ochre. Height channels use a schematic 45 degree elevation.";
